# Backend Update Guide: Tournament Image Upload

To support the image upload feature on the frontend, the backend `POST /tournements` endpoint needs to be updated to handle `multipart/form-data` requests.

## 1. Install Dependencies
Ensure you have `multer` (for handling file uploads) installed in your backend project.
```bash
npm install --save @nestjs/platform-express multer
# OR if using plain Express
npm install --save multer
```

## 2. Update the Controller (NestJS Example)

If your backend is built with **NestJS**, you need to use the `FileInterceptor`.

### `tournaments.controller.ts`

```typescript
import { 
  Controller, 
  Post, 
  UseInterceptors, 
  UploadedFile, 
  Body, 
  BadRequestException 
} from '@nestjs/common';
import { FileInterceptor } from '@nestjs/platform-express';
import { diskStorage } from 'multer';
import { extname } from 'path';

// ... other imports

@Post()
@UseInterceptors(FileInterceptor('file', {
  storage: diskStorage({
    destination: './uploads/tournaments', // Ensure this directory exists
    filename: (req, file, cb) => {
      const randomName = Array(32).fill(null).map(() => (Math.round(Math.random() * 16)).toString(16)).join('');
      return cb(null, `${randomName}${extname(file.originalname)}`);
    }
  }),
  fileFilter: (req, file, cb) => {
    if (!file.mimetype.match(/\/(jpg|jpeg|png|gif)$/)) {
      return cb(new BadRequestException('Only image files are allowed!'), false);
    }
    cb(null, true);
  }
}))
async create(
  @Body() createTournamentDto: CreateTournamentDto,
  @UploadedFile() file: Express.Multer.File
) {
  // If a file was uploaded, set the bannerImageUrl in the DTO
  if (file) {
    // Construct the public URL for the file
    // Adjust logic based on how you serve static files
    createTournamentDto.bannerImageUrl = `${process.env.API_URL}/uploads/tournaments/${file.filename}`;
  }

  return this.tournamentsService.create(createTournamentDto);
}
```

## 3. Update the Controller (Express Example)

If your backend is built with plain **Express**, use the `multer` middleware.

### `tournaments.routes.ts`

```typescript
import multer from 'multer';
import path from 'path';

// Configure storage
const storage = multer.diskStorage({
  destination: function (req, file, cb) {
    cb(null, 'uploads/tournaments'); // Ensure directory exists
  },
  filename: function (req, file, cb) {
    cb(null, Date.now() + path.extname(file.originalname));
  }
});

const upload = multer({ storage: storage });

// Apply middleware to route
router.post('/', upload.single('file'), async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const tournamentData = req.body;
    
    // If file uploaded, add to data
    if (req.file) {
      tournamentData.bannerImageUrl = `${process.env.API_URL}/uploads/tournaments/${req.file.filename}`;
    }

    const newTournament = await tournamentService.create(tournamentData);
    res.status(201).json(newTournament);
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(400).json({ message: error.message });
  }
});
```

## 4. Why This Failed Previously
The error `name should not be empty...` occurred because the backend was trying to parse the request body as JSON, but the frontend was sending `multipart/form-data`. Without the `multer` middleware (or `FileInterceptor`), the backend cannot parse the multipart body, resulting in an empty body object and triggering validation errors for all required fields.
